{
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  // 2026-11-18 - GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf (picomatch ReDoS through single-branch
  // repeated extglobs).  No patched picomatch release on npm: latest is 4.0.7
  // and the advisory's affected range is <=4.0.7 with first_patched_version
  // null.  The advisory was updated 2026-11-17, which is what turned
  // previously green main red - no repo change caused it.  Every lockfile
  // path is build- or test-time tooling running the project's own static
  // glob patterns, never attacker-controlled input: vitest/vite/tinyglobby
  // (test), typescript-eslint and eslint-config-next/fast-glob (lint), and
  // @sentry/nextjs sourcemap-upload bundler plugins (build).  Do not clear
  // with the semver-major vitest downgrade npm suggests (3.1.4): no
  // picomatch release fixes the advisory, so no dependency bump can.
  //
  // 2026-11-22 (MM) - status of the picomatch entry: GitHub withdrew
  // GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf on 2026-11-18 (advisory title "Withdrawn Advisory:
  // picomatch vulnerable to ReDoS through single-branch repeated extglobs";
  // withdrawn_at 2026-11-18T15:38:56Z; withdrawn because it is not a security
  // issue).  npm no longer reports it, so the entry is currently inert: the
  // audit passes at high severity with an empty allowlist as of this commit.
  // The entry stays so a republished advisory under the same GHSA cannot turn
  // main red again, and it costs nothing while it is inert.
  // Re-review if the advisory is republished or picomatch publishes a patch.
  //
  // 2026-11-18 - dropped the 2026-10-05 braces entry (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm).
  // That advisory is withdrawn (GitHub advisory title: "Withdrawn Advisory:
  // braces vulnerable to stack-exhaustion denial of service..."; no
  // firstPatchedVersion).  audit-ci no longer matches it, even though
  // braces 3.0.3 remains in the lockfile.  A stale allowlist entry would
  // silently suppress a future braces advisory if this GHSA were reused
  // or reopened.  Re-review if the advisory is republished.
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": ["GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf"]
}
